{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_architecture", "label": "docs/architecture.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_generated_app_js_bundle", "label": "Generated app.js bundle (classic script IIFE)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Source is ES modules under src/ so it can be unit-tested in Node; the build concatenates them into one classic script so index.html works when opened from file:// as well as over HTTP. Consequences: unique top-level names across modules (build fails loudly), only relative ./x.js imports and named export declarations, app.js regenerated after every src/ change and never edited by hand."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_module_dependency_order", "label": "Module dependency order sections->checks->config-parser->broker->analyzers->checklist->xlsx->report->ui->main", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The bundle is a plain concatenation with one shared scope, so lower modules must never import higher ones; ORDER in scripts/build.mjs encodes the same sequence."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_data_flow_pipeline", "label": "Data flow: file -> classifyFile -> detectHostname -> broker -> buildProfile -> buildChecklist/analyzeCheck -> UI table + buildWorkbook", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_analyzer_contract", "label": "Analyzer contract: ANALYZERS[ref] = (ctx) => result(...) | null", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ctx = { check, profile, profiles, targets, now }. Returning null falls back to defaultOutcome (Info dump of found sections, or Missing with a hint about gather-diagnostics vs supplemental). Analyzer exceptions are caught and surfaced as Info with an 'Analyzer error' note so one bad regex never blanks a whole column."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_section_extraction", "label": "CLI section extraction (gather-diagnostics headers + prompt transcripts)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "parseSections recognises two formats in the same file: '# CLI command:' header blocks and 'hostname> show ...' prompt lines. Sections are keyed by the normalised command; a check's commands may list '|' alternatives with first match wins. Supplemental transcripts are merged over diagnostics and profile.sectionSources records provenance so the UI can label the source."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_broker_profile", "label": "Broker profile (role, version, snapshot, management IPs, config facts)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Role from 'show redundancy detail' (Configuration Status Disabled -> Standalone, Operating Mode Monitoring Node -> Monitor, Active-Standby Role Primary/Backup) falling back to the '*' row of 'show redundancy group'; columns sorted Primary, Backup, Monitor. A router-name mismatch between config and diagnostics becomes a profile warning shown on the card and in the Summary sheet."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_snapshot_reference_date", "label": "Diagnostics snapshot time as reference date", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Certificate expiry and days-remaining are computed against the diagnostics snapshot ('Last Refreshed' from show storage-element * detail, then SMRP/SEMP/RDP log timestamps), not today's date, because the bundle may be reviewed long after capture; ctx.now is only the fallback and the 1.8.2 output says which reference date applied."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_config_redaction", "label": "Credential redaction at parse time (redactLine in parseConfig)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Password, secret and key values are masked while the current-config tree is built, before anything can reach the results table, the workbook or dev-script logs; never bypassed."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_config_tree_path_facts", "label": "Indentation-tree config parser with explicit-path facts", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "parseConfig builds a tree from two-space indentation, ignores 'exit' lines and collects '!' comments separately ('! Router:' gives the router name). Every fact is read from an explicit path so the shutdown of a client-username is never confused with the shutdown of a message-vpn."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_minimal_xlsx_writer", "label": "Minimal XLSX/ZIP writer", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "xlsx.js knows nothing about the checklist: it writes inline strings, sanitises XML-invalid characters, truncates to Excel's 32,767-character cell limit, freezes two header rows and two columns, and puts the autofilter on row 2 (so no vertical merges there). Deliberately minimal (fixed styles, no formulas) so it needs no dependency and opens in Excel and LibreOffice."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_soft_red_fail_fill", "label": "Fail uses a soft red fill", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fill colours follow the Solace 2025 palette; the palette has no red, so Fail deliberately uses a soft red in both workbook fills and UI pills."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_add_a_check_walkthrough", "label": "Adding a check walkthrough", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Row in CHECKS (unique three-segment ref, '|' command alternatives) -> ANALYZERS[ref] -> add to GATHER_DIAGNOSTICS_COMMANDS only if the standard bundle produces it (otherwise it joins the supplemental list automatically) -> fixture section + assertion in analyzers.test.js -> scripts/dev.sh all."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_add_a_broker_form", "label": "Add a broker form (one broker at a time)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "cli-diagnostics.txt required plus optional current-config export; hostname read from diagnostics and editable; a 'config' file that is really CLI output is attached as a supplemental transcript instead."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_bulk_import", "label": "Bulk import of gather-diagnostics folders", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kind and hostname detected per file so primary, backup and monitor bundles can be dropped together; system folders (usr/, var/, tmp/) and binary files are skipped; both paths converge on the same attach() call."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_assignment_tray", "label": "Assignment tray for files without a detected hostname", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "index_html_app_root", "target": "ui_createapp", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_generated_app_js_bundle", "target": "docs_architecture_module_dependency_order", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "scripts_lint", "target": "docs_architecture_generated_app_js_bundle", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readiness_run", "target": "scripts_serve", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_data_flow_pipeline", "target": "broker_classifyfile", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_data_flow_pipeline", "target": "broker_detecthostname", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_architecture_data_flow_pipeline", "target": "broker_buildprofile", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture